{"date": "2026-11-17", "piece": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide#Filter hooks with matchers", "client": "claude-code", "version": "", "url": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide", "row": "Hooks in the `hooks` key of settings files (2026-11-15)", "title": "Hook `if` field stops hooks on non-tool events", "effect": "wrong-data", "severity": "major", "sure": false, "why": "hook_items in base.py makes an item for every event group in settings['hooks'] and never inspects the handlers' `if` field or the event type. A hook the client now refuses to run is still shown as active.", "issue": "", "kitden": "b6a3d7c5efbb82067f8216f90707c24a43396cca"}
{"date": "2026-11-17", "piece": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/cli-reference#plugin install", "client": "claude-code", "version": "", "url": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/cli-reference", "row": "These commands work with no account: `claude --version`, `claude mcp add-json`, `get`, `list` and `remove`, `claude plugin validate --strict`, `marketplace add` and `remove`, `install`, `list --json`, `disable`, `enable` and `uninstall`; seen on Linux (2026-11-15, version 2.1.325). The nightly installs it with its own installer, `https://claude.ai/install.sh` run by `bash`, which puts `claude` in `~/.local/bin` and writes `~/.claude.json` with no account (2026-11-15, version 2.1.325, Linux)", "title": "Claude Code plugin install refused without a TTY for command-source plugins", "effect": "outdated", "severity": "minor", "sure": false, "why": "plugin_install_step deliberately omits -y so a plugin that installs by running a command stops; the new refusal matches that intent, so Kitden stays right, but the row's blanket claim and the code comment about how it stops are now less precise.", "issue": "", "kitden": "b6a3d7c5efbb82067f8216f90707c24a43396cca"}
{"date": "2026-11-17", "piece": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/cli-reference#plugin uninstall", "client": "claude-code", "version": "", "url": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/cli-reference", "row": "`claude plugin uninstall <id> -s <scope> --keep-data --json`; it fails while settings still switch the plugin on", "title": "Plugin uninstall reports settings_still_on when settings still enable the plugin", "effect": "outdated", "severity": "minor", "sure": true, "why": "plugin_remove_step uses the same flags (-s, --keep-data, --json) and the same settings key as before, so the command still works. Only the comment about the failure behaviour is now less precise (it omits the failureCode settings_still_on and the v2.1.282 requirement).", "issue": "", "kitden": "b6a3d7c5efbb82067f8216f90707c24a43396cca"}
{"date": "2026-11-17", "piece": "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#`config.toml`", "client": "codex", "version": "", "url": "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference", "row": "Settings folder is `CODEX_HOME`, default `~/.codex`; settings in `config.toml`", "title": "Codex profile config files next to config.toml", "effect": "unknown", "severity": "minor", "sure": false, "why": "scan() reads only config.toml under codex_home. The quote does not say what a profile file can contain or how it merges, so a concrete wrong value cannot be named. The default config.toml behavior is unchanged.", "issue": "", "kitden": "b6a3d7c5efbb82067f8216f90707c24a43396cca"}
